### 1. The Production Architecture (Feature-First Clean Architecture)

Junior devs dump API calls, money math, and UI inside `StatefulWidget`. Over-engineers create 15 abstract files just to render a button. Real production Flutter apps use **Pragmatic Feature-First Clean Architecture**:

```text
lib/
├── main.dart                                   # Entry point, ProviderScope, system chrome
├── core/
│   ├── theme/
│   │   └── app_theme.dart                      # Design tokens via ThemeExtension (OLED Dark)
│   └── utils/
│       └── money_formatter.dart                # Minor-unit integer currency formatting
└── features/
    └── cashflow/
        ├── domain/                             # 100% pure Dart (zero Flutter imports)
        │   ├── entities/subscription.dart      # Immutable model + billing math
        │   └── repositories/cashflow_repository.dart
        ├── data/                               # Persistence boundary (swap to Drift/SQLite anytime)
        │   └── repositories/local_cashflow_repository.dart
        └── presentation/                       # Riverpod state + 120fps interactive UI
            ├── controllers/cashflow_controller.dart
            ├── screens/dashboard_screen.dart
            └── widgets/
                ├── interactive_burn_dial.dart  # CustomPainter + touch-angle scrubbing + haptics
                ├── subscription_card.dart      # Swipe-to-simulate + press physics
                └── add_subscription_sheet.dart # Tactile composer modal
```

#### 4 Veteran Engineering Rules Built Into This Code:
1. **Never use `double` for money.** Floating-point math causes rounding bugs (`0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004`). Every monetary amount in VaultFlow is stored as integer minor units (`int amountCents`).
2. **Tabular numerals (`FontFeature.tabularFigures()`).** When numbers animate up/down during scrubbing or simulation, proportional fonts jitter horizontally. Tabular figures lock digit widths like a Swiss watch.
3. **Modern Flutter APIs only.** Uses wide-gamut `.withValues(alpha: ...)` (instead of deprecated `.withOpacity()`), `CardThemeData`, and modern Riverpod `NotifierProvider` (compatible with Riverpod 2.x & 3.x).
4. **Zero-friction swap for persistence.** The `CashflowRepository` interface decouples your UI from storage—run immediately today, then plug in **Drift (SQLite)** or **SQLCipher** without touching a single widget.

